      {
        "review_id": 364539187,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r364539187-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "75% of the country is Hindu so go to the main Hindu temple!",
        "text": "Seeing as 75% of the country is Hindu it makes sense to go to this beautiful temple. It is very busy every day but generally follow the crowds and you will be ok. The site is free entry so don't expect to pay for anything unless a guide picks you out. I didn't have a guide so wasn't able to learn much about the site. Unfortunately the main temple is strictly for Hindu people only. Go around the back of the main site across the river and you can watch the emotional and religious cremation of the recently deceased. It is a very interesting and touching to watch. From there I recommend going up the steps as there are plenty of photos to be taken. Keep an eye on your possessions as the monkeys (yes, actual monkeys) are very sneaky.",
